     "body": "<p>The desired behavior appears to be implemented. Creating resources using POST and PUT with text/turtle bodies with defined prefixes resulted in those prefixes being registered in the repository. Furthermore, the documentation for 5.x has been updated to reflect this behavior: <a href=\"https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FEDORA5x/Best+Practices+-+RDF+Namespaces\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FEDORA5x/Best+Practices+-+RDF+Namespaces</a></p>\n\n<p>Note, however, that depending in the outcome of \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"FCREPO-2785\" >\n                <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-2785\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\"  title=\"Stop using Modeshape Namespace registry\" >\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10300?size=medium\" />\n            FCREPO-2785\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Closed</span>\n            </span>\n, this may no longer be of as much concern.</p>",
     "created": "01/Oct/18 12:47 PM",
