  "description": "<p>This task is to ensure that RDF prefixes that are defined in PUT and POST requests as new Containers are registered within Fedora.</p>\n\n<p>For example, the following request should result in the registration of both the 'pcdm' and 'bibo' prefixes.<br/>\n&#8212; body.ttl<br/>\n@prefix pcdm: &lt;<a href=\"http://pcdm.org/models#\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://pcdm.org/models#</a>&gt; .<br/>\n@prefix bibo: &lt;<a href=\"http://purl.org/ontology/bibo/\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://purl.org/ontology/bibo/</a>&gt; .</p>\n\n<p>&lt;&gt; a pcdm:Object ;<br/>\nbibo:shortTitle 'Fedora4 Site Initialization Page' .<br/>\n&#8212;<br/>\nRequest:<br/>\n&gt; curl -i -XPUT -H\"Content-Type: text/turtle\" --data-binary @body.ttl localhost:8080/rest/test</p>\n\n<p>Note: When this ticket is completed, the following wiki page should be updated: <a href=\"https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FEDORA4x/Best+Practices+-+RDF+Namespaces\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FEDORA4x/Best+Practices+-+RDF+Namespaces</a></p>",
